{"title":"Career Roadmap · Public Health Assistant","role":"Public Health Assistant","summary":"A Public Health Assistant supports public-health teams in delivering preventive and community-based health programmes.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Community Health / Health Assistant"},"about":[{"label":"Important","text":"“Public Health Assistant” is a broad entry-level public-health role. Responsibilities and eligibility vary across government departments, NGOs, hospitals and community-health programmes. Some positions may specifically require a public-health, nursing, health-science or other prescribed qualification."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Public Health Assistant supports public-health teams in delivering preventive and community-based health programmes."},{"type":"p","text":"The role is generally focused on field implementation, community outreach, health education, data collection, screening support, surveillance and programme coordination rather than independent clinical treatment."},{"type":"h","text":"Typical work areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Community health programmes"},{"text":"Disease prevention"},{"text":"Health screening"},{"text":"Immunization support"},{"text":"Maternal and child health"},{"text":"Nutrition programmes"},{"text":"Non-communicable disease screening"},{"text":"Communicable disease surveillance"},{"text":"Health awareness"},{"text":"Community surveys"},{"text":"Health data collection"},{"text":"Referral coordination"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Career Flow"},{"type":"h","text":"Allied Health / Community Health Education"},{"type":"h","text":"Community Field Training"},{"type":"h","text":"Health Programme Internship"},{"type":"h","text":"Public Health Assistant"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Public Health Assistant"},{"type":"h","text":"Community Health Coordinator"},{"type":